  "notes": "The completion of a financial transaction. A compound of {決|けつ} (settle) + {済|さい} (finish). More formal and technical than {支払|しはら}い (payment).\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {決済|けっさい}{方法|ほうほう}: payment method\n- {電子|でんし}{決済|けっさい}: electronic payment\n- キャッシュレス{決済|けっさい}: cashless payment\n- {決済|けっさい}{完了|かんりょう}: payment completed\n- {決済|けっさい}する: to complete a payment\n\nMODERN USAGE:\nVery common in e-commerce, fintech, and POS systems. QRコード{決済|けっさい} (QR code payment) has become widespread in Japan.\n\nHOMOPHONE:\n{決裁|けっさい} means \"approval/authorization\" (different kanji, different meaning).",
